From 1faae5f9c70282476d99fdd7e145e9a00cbed53f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eva <eva@eva-core>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:38:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] prefill: native Blackwell block-scaled MoE GEMMs +
 env-gated FP8 dense projections

MoE grouped GEMMs (wgemm.cu): optional native path (MoeAct a.q/a.s, dispatched
when set) feeding the checkpoint's own NVFP4/MXFP8 codes and block scales
straight into sm_120a tensor cores - mxf4nvf4 m16n8k64 ue4m3 for layers 0-19,
mxf8f6f4 m16n8k32 ue8m0 for layers 20-23 - with per-row dynamic activation
quantization (moe_quant.cu) and the per-expert factor applied to the FP32
accumulator. BF16 legacy path unchanged in the same binary.

Measured (interleaved, same binary, INGINE_PREFILL_FP4_MOE): 4K +31.1%,
32K +27.6%, 131K +21.3% prefill tok/s; TTFT -16%; needles 4/4 at 32K and
131K with identical retrieved codes; greedy output changes (lossy activation
quantization). 20-prompt decode panel: no systematic regression.

Dense wproj/wo FP8 path (gemm.cpp run_fp8 + gemm_fp8.cu): per-row E4M3
activation quant + checkpoint FP8 rows into cuBLASLt E4M3xE4M3 with a
row x column scale epilogue, gated by INGINE_PREFILL_FP8_DENSE. +4-5%
prefill, rejected as default (fixed-panel decode -3.8%, greedy drift);
kept for a future retest.

Verified by standalone tests: /tmp/e3/{nvfp4_mma_test,wgemm_cpu_check,
mxfp8_check,wgemm_native_test}.cu - exact-semantics CPU references, 0
mismatches across formats, GEMMs and T=4..600.
